    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what u mean about reform, but it feels like the mainstream media is always trying to dismiss these concerns as just \"rhetoric\" to protect the status quo. if the corruption is actually as widespread as people claim, shouldn't we stop calling it rhetoric and start calling it what it is? wouldn't it be more accurate to say that the movement is simply reacting to an undeniable reality?",
