      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is certainly true that strong, well-grounded critiques of power and systemic bias are a fundamental part of political discourse and are not inherently \"rhetoric.\"\n\nHowever, the difference often lies in the *evidence presented and the proposed solutions for change*, not the initial feeling of being wronged.\n\nWhen powerful claims are consistently labeled \"rhetoric,\" it often suggests the mainstream perspective believes the claims are **unsubstantiable in a comprehensive political sense,** not just that the *feeling* is inaccurate.",
